#   - Interception layer for probe 3: engine routing block (engine.py),
#     BEFORE the fan-in node runs -- the FanInHandler never executes.
#   - numstat: +32/-1 across 1 file
#
# The two shapes are OPPOSITE in probe 3 mechanism:
#   A: intercepts INSIDE the fan-in node handler (fan_in.py) -- the
#      fan-in node runs but its handler short-circuits.
#   D: intercepts BEFORE the fan-in node runs (engine.py routing block)
#      -- the fan-in node never executes at all.
#
# Additional structural differences:
#   A: touches two files (engine.py, handlers/fan_in.py)
#   D: touches one file (engine.py), two hunks at different sites
#
#   A: probe 3 fix lives in the fan-in aggregation layer
#   D: probe 3 fix lives in the engine routing layer
#
#   A: the fan-in node's execution is reached but short-circuited
#   D: the fan-in node's execution is bypassed entirely by the engine
#
# ============================================================================
# WHY PROBE 1 PASSES (conditional-mismatch dead end, run_subgraph)
# ============================================================================
#
# DEAD_END_NODE succeeds; its only outgoing edge has condition="outcome=fail".
# run_subgraph calls select_edge(DEAD_END_NODE, ...) => returns None.
# Hunk 1 (run_subgraph): outgoing_edges(DEAD_END_NODE) returns [the
#   condition=fail edge] (non-empty) => returns Outcome(FAIL, failure_reason=
#   "Subgraph dead end at 'DEAD_END_NODE': no outgoing edge matched
#   outcome='success'").
# Probe 1 asserts status==FAIL with non-empty failure_reason AND node ran
# exactly once => PASSES.
#
# ============================================================================
# WHY PROBE 2 PASSES (mixed-scope / whole-scope suppression guard)
# ============================================================================
#
# GOOD_NODE succeeds; its outgoing edge is unconditional.
# run_subgraph calls select_edge(GOOD_NODE, ...) => returns the unconditional
# edge (not None). Hunk 1's outgoing_edges() branch is never reached.
# run_subgraph advances to GOOD_EXIT_NODE (shape=Msquare, is_exit_node()=True).
# On the next loop iteration, is_exit_node() fires and returns last_outcome
# (SUCCESS) BEFORE select_edge is called for GOOD_EXIT_NODE.
# Probe 2 asserts status==SUCCESS => PASSES.
#
# ============================================================================
# WHY PROBE 3 PASSES (composed parent outcome, parallel branch surface)
# ============================================================================
#
# Probe 3 graph has a valid fan-in topology: both branches have a graph-level
# path to PAR_FAN_IN (PAR_DEAD_BRANCH -> PAR_DEAD_NEXT -> PAR_FAN_IN and
# PAR_GOOD_BRANCH -> PAR_FAN_IN). _find_fan_in_node() succeeds.
#
# At runtime:
#   1. Engine runs PAR_FAN_OUT (shape=component) via ParallelHandler.
#   2. ParallelHandler runs both branches via run_subgraph:
#      - PAR_DEAD_BRANCH: succeeds; only outgoing edge has condition="outcome=fail"
#        => select_edge returns None; outgoing_edges() is non-empty =>
#        Hunk 1 returns Outcome(FAIL, failure_reason="Subgraph dead end at ...").
#      - PAR_GOOD_BRANCH: succeeds; unconditional edge to PAR_FAN_IN
#        (shape=tripleoctagon) => is_exit_node() fires at PAR_FAN_IN =>
#        run_subgraph returns SUCCESS.
#   3. _apply_join_policy(wait_all): 1 SUCCESS + 1 FAIL => returns
#      Outcome(PARTIAL_SUCCESS, ...).
#   4. ParallelHandler returns PARTIAL_SUCCESS to engine (stored in `outcome`).
#   5. Engine: current_node.shape == "component", len(all_branches) > 1.
#   6. _find_fan_in_node() => PAR_FAN_IN (not None).
#   7. Hunk 2: outcome.status == PARTIAL_SUCCESS != SUCCESS =>
#      _emit_complete(outcome, ...) and return outcome (PARTIAL_SUCCESS).
#   8. par_outcome.status == PARTIAL_SUCCESS != SUCCESS => probe 3 PASSES.
#
# Note: PAR_DEAD_NEXT never runs (PAR_DEAD_BRANCH dead-ends before reaching
# it), so the probe's PAR_DEAD_NEXT count check (== 0) also passes.
#
# ============================================================================
# WHY THIS IS STILL A CRUDE STUB (NOT A CORRECT FIX)
# ============================================================================
#
# Hunk 1 (run_subgraph dead-end detection):
#   - Same crudeness as shape A hunk 1 (see hypothesis.patch for full list).
#   - Does not update context/engine-semantics.md §3 or specs/EXTENSIONS.md §33.
#   - Does not update tests/test_subgraph_runner.py::test_run_from_stops_at_dead_end.
#   - Does not emit PIPELINE_ERROR events from run_subgraph.
#
# Hunk 2 (component routing short-circuit):
#   - Wrong layer: the engine's routing block is not the right place to gate
#     on branch health.  The fan-in node exists precisely to aggregate branch
#     results; bypassing it entirely removes all fan-in aggregation logic
#     (LLM evaluation, heuristic selection, context recording of best_id/
#     best_status/best_outcome).
#   - Breaks legitimate use cases: a pipeline that uses a fan-in node to
#     explicitly handle partial failures (e.g. "select the best result even
#     if some branches failed") will never run its fan-in node when any
#     branch fails.  This is a broader breakage than shape A's fan_in.py
#     stub, which at least runs the fan-in node before short-circuiting.
#   - The returned outcome has failure_reason=None (from _apply_join_policy's
#     PARTIAL_SUCCESS return); a correct fix would surface the dead-end
#     failure_reason from the failed branch.
#   - No doc, spec, or test updates for the new routing behavior.
#   - _emit_complete is called with the PARTIAL_SUCCESS outcome, not a proper
#     FAIL outcome; the pipeline events stream will show PARTIAL_SUCCESS as
#     the final status, which is misleading.
#
# A correct fix would:
#   1. Keep detection in run_subgraph (engine.py) for the dead-end case.
#   2. Propagate the dead-end failure_reason through parallel.results so the
#      fan-in node can see it and aggregate correctly.
#   3. Update the fan-in node's aggregation logic to treat a dead-end branch
#      as a hard failure (not just a lower-ranked candidate).
#   4. Update context/engine-semantics.md §3 and specs/EXTENSIONS.md §33.
#   5. Update tests/test_subgraph_runner.py::test_run_from_stops_at_dead_end.
#
